# Semgrep ignore list.
#
# Picked up automatically by `semgrep scan .` — both the CI SAST job
# (.github/workflows/security.yml) and local runs. Excludes non-first-party
# and generated files so the scan is faster (relevant to Actions cost) and the
# findings list is not drowned in false positives from dependencies / build
# artifacts. First-party source (server/, frontend/app, frontend/lib,
# frontend/components, agent/, deploy/) is still fully scanned.

# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
vendor/

# ── Build output / caches ────────────────────────────────────
.next/
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
bin/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Generated code (reviewed at its source, not the .pb.go) ──
*.pb.go
*.pb.gw.go
*_grpc.pb.go

# ── Minified / bundled assets ────────────────────────────────
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.bundle.js

# ── Lockfiles (hashes trigger secret/entropy false positives) ─
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
go.sum

# ── Binaries / archives ──────────────────────────────────────
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.gz

# ── Test fixtures (intentional dummy secrets / sample payloads) ─
**/testdata/
